{"task_id": "HumanEval/55", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import Dict\n\nclass FibonacciCalculator:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self._memo: Dict[int, int] = {0: 0, 1: 1}\n\n    def calculate(self, n: int) -> int:\n        if n < 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"Input 'n' must be a non-negative integer.\")\n        if n not in self._memo:\n            # Iterative approach for better performance and avoiding recursion depth limits.\n            a, b = 0, 1\n            for i in range(2, n + 1):\n                if i not in self._memo:\n                    self._memo[i] = a + b\n                a, b = b, self._memo[i]\n        return self._memo[n]\n\n_calculator = FibonacciCalculator()\n\ndef fib(n: int):\n    \"\"\"Return n-th Fibonacci number.\n    >>> fib(10)\n    55\n    >>> fib(1)\n    1\n    >>> fib(8)\n    21\n    \"\"\"\n    return _calculator.calculate(n)\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/57", "solution": "```python\ndef monotonic(l: list):\n    \"\"\"Return True is list elements are monotonically increasing or decreasing.\n    >>> monotonic([1, 2, 4, 20])\n    True\n    >>> monotonic([1, 20, 4, 10])\n    False\n    >>> monotonic([4, 1, 0, -10])\n    True\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(l) <= 1:\n        return True\n\n    def _is_increasing(lst: list) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Checks if a list is monotonically increasing.\"\"\"\n        for i in range(len(lst) - 1):\n            if lst[i] > lst[i+1]:\n                return False\n        return True\n\n    def _is_decreasing(lst: list) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Checks if a list is monotonically decreasing.\"\"\"\n        for i in range(len(lst) - 1):\n            if lst[i] < lst[i+1]:\n                return False\n        return True\n\n    return _is_increasing(l) or _is_decreasing(l)\n```"}
