{"task_id": "HumanEval/148", "solution": "```python\ndef bf(planet1, planet2):\n    '''\n    There are eight planets in our solar system: the closerst to the Sun\n    is Mercury, the next one is Venus, then Earth, Mars, Jupiter, Saturn,\n    Uranus, Neptune.\n    Write a function that takes two planet names as strings planet1 and planet2.\n    The function should return a tuple containing all planets whose orbits are\n    located between the orbit of planet1 and the orbit of planet2, sorted by\n    the proximity to the sun.\n    The function should return an empty tuple if planet1 or planet2\n    are not correct planet names.\n    Examples\n    bf(\"Jupiter\", \"Neptune\") ==> (\"Saturn\", \"Uranus\")\n    bf(\"Earth\", \"Mercury\") ==> (\"Venus\")\n    bf(\"Mercury\", \"Uranus\") ==> (\"Venus\", \"Earth\", \"Mars\", \"Jupiter\", \"Saturn\")\n    '''\n    SOLAR_SYSTEM_PLANETS = [\n        \"Mercury\", \"Venus\", \"Earth\", \"Mars\",\n        \"Jupiter\", \"Saturn\", \"Uranus\", \"Neptune\"\n    ]\n\n    def get_planet_index(planet_name, planets_list_local):\n        \"\"\"Returns the 0-based index of a planet or None if not found.\"\"\"\n        try:\n            return planets_list_local.index(planet_name)\n        except ValueError:\n            return None\n\n    idx1 = get_planet_index(planet1, SOLAR_SYSTEM_PLANETS)\n    idx2 = get_planet_index(planet2, SOLAR_SYSTEM_PLANETS)\n\n    if idx1 is None or idx2 is None:\n        return ()\n\n    start_idx = min(idx1, idx2)\n    end_idx = max(idx1, idx2)\n\n    # Slice the list to get planets strictly between the two input planets.\n    intermediate_planets = SOLAR_SYSTEM_PLANETS[start_idx + 1:end_idx]\n\n    return tuple(intermediate_planets)\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/147", "solution": "def get_max_triples(n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts triples (a[i], a[j], a[k]) with i < j < k where a[i] + a[j] + a[k] is a multiple of 3.\n    a[x] = x*x - x + 1.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def combinations(n_val, k_val):\n        \"\"\"Calculates 'n choose k', the number of combinations.\"\"\"\n        if k_val < 0 or k_val > n_val:\n            return 0\n        if k_val == 0 or k_val == n_val:\n            return 1\n        if k_val > n_val // 2:\n            k_val = n_val - k_val\n\n        res = 1\n        for i in range(k_val):\n            res = res * (n_val - i) // (i + 1)\n        return res\n\n    # Analyze a[x] = x*x - x + 1 modulo 3:\n    # If x % 3 == 0: a[x] = 0*(-1) + 1 = 1 (mod 3)\n    # If x % 3 == 1: a[x] = 1*(0) + 1 = 1 (mod 3)\n    # If x % 3 == 2: a[x] = 2*(1) + 1 = 3 = 0 (mod 3)\n    # So, a[x] % 3 is 0 if x % 3 is 2, and 1 otherwise.\n\n    count_mod_0_a = 0 # count of a[x] where a[x] % 3 == 0 (i.e., x % 3 == 2)\n    count_mod_1_a = 0 # count of a[x] where a[x] % 3 == 1 (i.e., x % 3 == 0 or x % 3 == 1)\n\n    for x in range(1, n + 1):\n        if x % 3 == 2:\n            count_mod_0_a += 1\n        else: # x % 3 == 0 or x % 3 == 1\n            count_mod_1_a += 1\n\n    # For a sum (rem1 + rem2 + rem3) to be 0 (mod 3), given remainders can only be 0 or 1:\n    # It must be (0 + 0 + 0) or (1 + 1 + 1).\n\n    # Count triples where all three elements have remainder 0 (mod 3)\n    triples_from_mod_0 = combinations(count_mod_0_a, 3)\n\n    # Count triples where all three elements have remainder 1 (mod 3)\n    triples_from_mod_1 = combinations(count_mod_1_a, 3)\n\n    return triples_from_mod_0 + triples_from_mod_1"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/150", "solution": "import math\n\ndef x_or_y(n, x, y):\n    \"\"\"A simple program which should return the value of x if n is\n    a prime number and should return the value of y otherwise.\n\n    Examples:\n    for x_or_y(7, 34, 12) == 34\n    for x_or_y(15, 8, 5) == 5\n\n    \"\"\"\n    def _is_prime(num):\n        # Checks if an integer is a prime number.\n        if num <= 1:\n            return False\n        if num == 2:\n            return True\n        if num % 2 == 0:\n            return False\n\n        # Iterates from 3 up to the square root of num, checking for odd divisors.\n        for i in range(3, int(math.sqrt(num)) + 1, 2):\n            if num % i == 0:\n                return False\n        return True\n\n    if _is_prime(n):\n        return x\n    else:\n        return y"}
